#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1063 expect=noViolation domain=AE
#note "Mirrors rulespec PMDA-SD1063-declared.yaml - the NON-FIRING arm of the A/B pair. The Define-XML declares BOTH submitted datasets, so nothing is missing and the correct answer is zero violations. This is the guard against the one input shape that produces a silently WRONG verdict rather than a skip: a define_dataset_names() that degraded to an EMPTY list would make 'ds_name(DATA) not in $define_datasets' true for every dataset - the firing sibling would stay green (it expects a violation anyway) while THIS scenario goes 0 -> 1 and turns red."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#define-xml PMDA-SD1063-define-both.xml
dataset AE label="Adverse Events"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col AESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col AETERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Adverse Event"
---
S1 | AE | 001 | 1 | HEADACHE
---

dataset VS label="Vital Signs"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col VSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col VSTESTCD type=Char label="Vital Signs Test Short Name"
---
S1 | VS | 001 | 1 | SYSBP
